Title: Diagnosis of test `testNullCommentEqualsEmptyComment`
Details: The test creates three ZipArchiveEntry objects for the same file name "foo". It sets one entry's comment to null, one to an empty string, and the third to "bar". The test asserts that the entry with null comment equals the entry with empty comment.

Looking into the `ZipArchiveEntry.equals(Object)` method, it compares fields including the name and comment of the entries. The relevant snippet is:

```java
String myComment = getComment();
String otherComment = other.getComment();
if (myComment == null) {
    if (otherComment != null) {
        return false;
    }
} else if (!myComment.equals(otherComment)) {
    return false;
}
```

This means the entries are considered equal only if both comments are null or if the comments are equal strings. Since the method distinguishes between `null` and empty string (`""`), the equality comparison returns false when one entry has null comment and the other an empty comment, causing the test failure.

The test expects entries with null comment and empty comment to be considered equal, but current implementation regards them as different.

Suggestion: The equality method should be updated to treat `null` and empty comment as equivalent. This can be done by normalizing null comments to empty strings before comparison or adjusting the conditions to regard null and empty comments as equal.

The suspect method to fix is:

org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.zip.ZipArchiveEntry.equals(java.lang.Object)

